                        "type": "0",
                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "The nurse is caring for a client who is in the chronic phase of stroke (brain attack) and has a right-sided hemiparesis. The nurse identifies that the client is unable to feed self. Which is the appropriate nursing intervention?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "80db17ea97ed8fdcd1b6b9666390fca1",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Applying 应用",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nRight-sided hemiparesis is weakness of the right arm and leg. The nurse would teach the client to use both sides of the body to increase strength and build endurance. Providing a pureed diet is incorrect. The question does not mention swallowing difficulty, so there is no need to puree the food. Informing the client that a feeding tube may need to be placed is incorrect. That information would come from the primary health care provider. Providing a variety of foods is also incorrect because the problem is not the food selection but the client's ability to eat the food independently.",
                        "id": "09e2d0ee868444f391e70088809a0c03",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "5d06d34d69554ceeac75f270a95680e3",
                                "content": "Ask the family to deliver the care."
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "f4a5dbb7cae64c0594f755bb3d60c98a",
                                "content": "Leave the client alone until ready to participate."
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "bac35be541734a669755afad83a3841a",
                                "content": "Advise the client that rehabilitation progresses more quickly with cooperation."
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "0842bd6369f44d238562fc340ce6eaf8",
                                "content": "Acknowledge the client's anger and continue to encourage participation in care."
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "5d06d34d69554ceeac75f270a95680e3",
                                    "content": "Ask the family to deliver the care."
                                },
                                {
