                        "type": "0",
                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "A client who had a stroke (brain attack) has right-sided hemianopsia. What would the nurse plan to do to help the client adapt to this problem?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "80db17ea97ed8fdcd1b6b9666390fca1",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Applying 应用",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nHemianopsia is blindness in half of the visual field. The client with hemianopsia is taught to scan the environment. This allows the client to take in the entirety of the visual field, which is necessary for proper functioning within the environment and helps to prevent injury to the client. Options 2 and 3 will not help the client adapt to this visual impairment. Eyeglasses are useful if the client already wears them, but they will not correct this visual field deficit.",
                        "id": "24527984911044b7811b69093c18f164",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "3827c20f2c0a4cd5a3eeff03abb608de",
                                "content": "Had a very mild stroke"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "8a5c5dccff594a02b824b054da040456",
                                "content": "Most likely suffered a transient ischemic attack"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "20c1d2461cbf4351accd8c7d1fba74d4",
                                "content": "May have difficulty with language abilities only"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "df8e5ff152b34a85a5ef8e5bab0c8dfe",
                                "content": "Is likely to have perceptual and spatial disabilities"
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "3827c20f2c0a4cd5a3eeff03abb608de",
                                    "content": "Had a very mild stroke"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "8a5c5dccff594a02b824b054da040456",
                                    "content": "Most likely suffered a transient ischemic attack"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "20c1d2461cbf4351accd8c7d1fba74d4",
                                    "content": "May have difficulty with language abilities only"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "1",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "df8e5ff152b34a85a5ef8e5bab0c8dfe",
                                    "content": "Is likely to have perceptual and spatial disabilities"
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        "isSubmit": "0",
                        "delFlag": "0",
                        "type": "0",
                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "The nurse is caring for a client with a diagnosis of right (nondominant) hemispheric stroke. The nurse notes that the client is alert and oriented to time and place. On the basis of these assessment findings, the nurse would make which interpretation?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nThe client with a right (nondominant) hemispheric stroke may be alert and oriented to time and place. These signs of apparent wellness often suggest that the client is less disabled than is the case. However, impulsivity and confusion in carrying out activities may be very real problems for these clients as a result of perceptual and spatial disabilities. The right hemisphere is considered specialized in sensory-perceptual and visual-spatial processing and awareness of body space. The left hemisphere is dominant for language abilities.",
                        "id": "369e582a7abc47cdbd20f940aa51c11d",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "5e94ae2a841b40ed8039f600e298c1db",
                                "content": "Occipital lobe impairment"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "bf2a43e3ffa845a8887307669d11bc0c",
                                "content": "Damage to the auditory association areas"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "d8878af6585046419b9307f65dda700c",
                                "content": "Frontal lobe and optic nerve tracts damage"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "227bb7a43a2946ca99d61e6dff77a6c8",
                                "content": "Difficulty with concept formation and abstraction areas"
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "5e94ae2a841b40ed8039f600e298c1db",
                                    "content": "Occipital lobe impairment"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "1",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
